3. THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL — NOT covered by sections 1 and 2
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

3.1 UPSTREAM SOURCE DATASET

    Every measurement in this repository is derived from:

        Aygun, A.; Blaney, G.; Haga, Z.; McWilliams, T.; Mertens, J.;
        de Ruiter, J. P.; Ward, N.; Scheutz, M.
        "Multi-modal data acquisition platform for behavioral evaluation."
        Harvard Dataverse, 2024.  DOI: 10.7910/DVN/HMZ5RG

    That deposit is released under the Creative Commons CC0 1.0 Universal
    Public Domain Dedication:

        https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

    CC0 waives copyright and related rights worldwide, so the upstream
    measurements impose no licensing restriction on the derived features and
    analysis outputs distributed here, and section 2's CC BY 4.0 grant applies
    to them without qualification.

    CC0 carries no legal attribution requirement. Nevertheless, in line with
    the Harvard Dataverse community norms and ordinary scholarly practice, any
    use of this repository's data should cite the upstream deposit as given
    above, alongside this work (see CITATION.cff). Not citing it would be a
    breach of academic norms, not of a licence.

3.2 VENDORED UPSTREAM DOCUMENTATION

    docs/reference/Data description.txt

    This file is a verbatim copy of the source dataset's own documentation and
    is the work of the dataset authors listed in section 3.1, not of this
    repository's author. It is covered by the upstream CC0 1.0 dedication
    rather than by section 1 or section 2, and may therefore be redistributed
    freely; the citation expectation in section 3.1 applies to it as well.

3.3 IEEE LATEX CLASS FILES

    IEEEtran.cls, IEEEtran.bst, ieeeconf.cls and IEEEtran_HOWTO.pdf, wherever
    they appear (including inside the manuscript submodules and under
    docs/experiments/results/), are the property of the IEEE and are
    distributed under their own terms (LaTeX Project Public License / IEEE's
    own conditions). They are NOT covered by section 1 or section 2 and must
    not be redistributed as part of this work.

3.4 DEPENDENCIES

    Third-party Python packages listed in requirements.txt are neither vendored
    nor redistributed by this repository; each remains under its own licence
    (predominantly BSD, MIT and Apache-2.0). Importing them imposes no
